{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/923952-sidereals-wfhl-traits-of-the-sidereal-exalted-paradox-and-kismet","id":923952,"title":"[Sidereals:WFHL] Traits of the Sidereal Exalted - Paradox and Kismet","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Sidereal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-30T10:42:48-07:00","id":923952,"title":"[Sidereals:WFHL] Traits of the Sidereal Exalted - Paradox and Kismet","content":"<b>Chapter 4 : Traits of the Sidereal Exalted</b><br /> The Sidereal Exalted share a great deal with the Solars; they have common Attributes and Abilities, the same Health and Willpower tracks, as well as many of the same Merits and Flaws. Like the Solars, the Sidereals are divided into Castes, based upon which of the Maidens of Destiny chose them and which inform her role within the scheme of destiny. However, the Sidereal Exalted are not cursed in the fashion of the Lawgivers; your character does not have a Limit track, but rather is afflicted by Paradox, a measure of how snarled Fate has become due to her actions. Additionally, all Sidereals suffer from Arcane Fate, a lingering consequence of the Sidereals hiding their participation in the Usurpation from the world, resulting in the memory of Sidereals easily slipping away unless they don a Resplendent Destiny. Finally, the end of the chapter governs experience points and character advancement as a Sidereal.<br /> <br /> <b>Paradox</b><br /> <br /> Sidereals walk in the spaces between what was, what is, and what shall be- and it is not an easy walk. More than anyone else, the Chosen of the Maidens know how fragile the veil of reality can be, and how quickly it can be torn asunder. When the weave of Fate becomes tangled, strangeness begins to haunt the world and madness plagues her people. Where the weave is thin, the enemies of Heaven marshall their forces, awaiting a fatal tear through which they can march against Creation.<br /> <br /> And there is always the temptation- to punish the arrogant with eternal voyages, or trap someone in a home they would do anything to leave; to enjoy the attentions of a certain paramour, or see a rival's love turn sour; to see your people victorious in battle, or a blood feud settled on your terms; to learn forbidden secrets, or conceal darkest shames; to extend the life of a loved one, or cut the thread of an enemy short. To take Fate into one's own hands. <br /> <br /> Sidereals are invested with a great deal of discretion when it comes to such matters- as the Chosen of the Maidens of Destiny, it is assumed that they act in the interests of Heaven. As Rakan Thulio illustrated so long ago, such trust can be misplaced.<br /> <br /> Paradox is a measure of how twisted fate has become due to the Sidereal\u2019s actions. As a Sidereal accrues Paradox, they draw closer to suffering from a backlash, the tension between what was, is, and could be snaps, with often unpredictable results. When she reaches 10 Paradox, a backlash becomes inevitable, although one may occur before this point as well.<br /> <br /> The Sidereal Exalted gain Paradox in the following ways:<br /> <br /> * Once per scene, when a Sidereal acts in a way to violate a Major or Defining Intimacy of a Resplendent Destiny she is wearing (see below), her player rolls a single die, gaining one point of Paradox for each success.<br /> * Once per scene, when a Sidereal fails to uphold the known will of Heaven, her player rolls a single die, gaining one point of Paradox for each success (unless he has already acted directly against the known will of Heaven; see below). A Sidereal always knows if she will gain Paradox from failing to uphold the known will of Heaven; this should only occur when she specifically chooses not to enact her mission as assigned from the Bureau of Destiny.<br /> * Once per scene, when a Sidereal acts directly against the known will of Heaven, her player rolls two dice, gaining one point of Paradox for each success (or one die if she has already failed to uphold the known will of Heaven).<br /> * A small number of the Charms of the Sidereals potentially result in Paradox, especially when used too frequently within a short time.<br /> * Each Sidereal has a secret destiny, learned upon the moment of her Exaltation and selected during character creation. This destiny is known as her Kismet. Once per scene, when a Sidereal acts against her Kismet, her player rolls a three dice, gaining one point of Paradox for each success.<br /> <br /> <b>Resolving Paradox</b><br /> When a Sidereal ensures some especially legendary or unlikely design from the Bureau of Destiny comes to pass, she may reduce her Paradox by 1 at the Storyteller\u2019s discretion. Additionally, once per story, if the Sidereal spends at least one week in Creation, surrounded with her Acquaintances and without veiling her identity behind a Resplendent Destiny, she may roll (Acquaintances), reducing her Paradox by 1 per success. Finally, a Sidereal who permanently resolves her Kismet immediately reduces her Paradox to zero.<br /> <br /> <b>Examples of Kismet</b><br /> A Sidereal\u2019s Kismet should almost always relate to her Caste, and should generally be something that the player of the Sidereal is interested in exploring. The following examples of Kismet are intended to provide inspiration and examples, not to serve as an exhaustive list.<br /> Additionally, if a Sidereal\u2019s Kismet becomes impossible or meaningless, her player should work with the Storyteller to devise her new Kismet.<br /> <br /> At a narrative level, Heaven does to control a Sidereal\u2019s Kismet. Indeed, many within the Bureau of Destiny have been frustrated by a Sidereal\u2019s decision to go off mission in the service of her Kismet. Amongst the Sidereals, there is a general agreement that Kismet is the way destiny \u2018wants\u2019 to flow- but what that means and implies is, itself a subject of much discussion.<br /> <br /> At a play level, Kismet should not be a singular, overwhelming force in a Sidereal\u2019s life or activities, but rather a source of tension between what she personally wants (her intimacies), what her orders are (the known will of Heaven), and the natural flow of destiny in the world (her Kismet). <br /> <br /> What follows are some example Kismets, as well as a means to violate the Kismet and thus incur Paradox. <br /> <br /> <b>Examples of Kismet for the Chosen of Journeys</b><br /> * Ensure the prosperity of the Guild. (Freeing a caravan of guild slaves about to be sold to the Fair Folk.)<br /> * Cause a contented homebody to go on a bothersome adventure. (Encouraging that homebody they\u2019re better off staying at home, because they are your friend and adventures are dangerous.)<br /> * Allowing a wandering people to permanently settle down. (Assisting the people in finding a homeland of their own.)<br /> <br /> <b>Examples of Kismet for the Chosen of Serenity</b><br /> * Bring together two children of rival houses, both alike in dignity. (Fall in love with and abduct one of them for yourself.)<br /> * Inspire an artist to produce one of the great works of art for the Age. (Producing the work yourself and passing it off as that of the artist\u2019s.)<br /> * Ensure that a specific bloodline is propagated through the years. (Assisting a pretender to the lineage, in order to prevent civil war from breaking out.)<br /> <br /> <b>Examples of Kismet for the Chosen of Battles</b><br /> * Mentor a stripling into being a hero- or a villain. (Training your would-be hero in the art of poison and assassination to be more effective, or killing your would-be villain to save the lives of their victims.)<br /> * Ensure that an ambitious noble oversteps, igniting a civil war. (Assist that noble behind the scenes, such that they rise to power without civil war breaking out)<br /> * Safeguard a man such that he does not fall until his appointed battle. (The man you guard is a monster who richly deserves his death)<br /> <br /> <b>Examples of Kismet for the Chosen of Secrets</b><br /> * Ensure that the lost heir of Lookshy remains lost but discoverable. (Allowing someone to accurately trace their lineage as the lost heir.)<br /> * Conceal the crimes of Heaven. (Reveal those crimes so that justice may be done)<br /> * Discover the secret truths that predate Creation. (Turn away from fear of the wrath of Orabilis)<br /> <br /> <b>Examples of Kismet for the Chosen of Endings</b><br /> * Bring the end of Gem. (Standing in defense of your adopted home, Gem)<br /> * Cure plagues only after they ravage the land (Refuse to stand idly by and watch as the innocent suffer)<br /> * Bring peace in a region ravaged by war. (The rebels will only stop fighting when some gruesome examples are made)<br /> <br /> <b>Backlash</b><br /> When a Sidereal gains one or more points of Paradox, the Storyteller should roll dice equal to her new Paradox rating. For each success, the Sidereal\u2019s Paradox is reduced by 1, and she suffers from a point of Backlash. If a Sidereal\u2019s Paradox would reach or exceed 10, then instead she suffers from a 10 point Backlash and reduces her Paradox to zero. The Storyteller should distribute these Backlash points across the following categories:<br /> <br /> <b>Causality Violation</b><br /> 1. Relatively minor violations of causality occur around you. Water flows backwards, flags flap in the wrong direction, milk curdles, candles burn in the color of your Maiden, flowers bloom or wilt out of season.<br /> 2. Severe but limited violations of causality occur around you. A contact you needed drowns on dry land. An acquaintance knowingly betrays you into the hands of your enemies.<br /> 3. Moderate violations of causality occur in a wide area around you. A drunken riot burns down a neighborhood, as the wine barrels refuse to empty. A bothersome fate aberration (p. XX) may occur.<br /> 4. Severe violations of causality occur in a very wide area around you. A prince's kingdom falls into civil war after his assassination, even though he is still alive. A dangerous fate aberration (p. XX) may occur.<br /> 5. Very severe violations of causality occur, potentially impacting the region forever. A volcano erupts from a mossy hill; a cyclone flattens a city from clear skies; a spell for clear weather suddenly creates unending drought. A powerful and antagonistic fate aberration (p. XX) may occur- potentially even catalyzing a Getimian Exaltation.<br /> <br /> <b>Incursion</b><br /> 1. A ghost, hobgoblin or unbound first circle demon enters Creation. Although they will not directly seek you out, their presence is likely to complicate your life.<br /> 2. As above, but the entity leaves behind a rift, allowing communication and possession, but not transportation forms between Creation and some other realm.<br /> 3. A larger incursion of up to half a dozen such spirits. Alternatively, a single more powerful entity may come through, such as a Fair Folk noble, a powerful nephwrack or a second circle demon.<br /> 4. Breakthrough; a region of Creation is lost to the Bordermarches, breaks into a Shadowland, or becomes a path to the Demon Realm. Malign influence is certain to seep in from such a thing.<br /> 5. Invasion; a region of Creation is sundered and claimed by the enemy- it falls to the middlemarches of the Wyld and a court of Fair Folk nobility, or becomes a Shadowland centered on a powerful and malicious ghostly force, or a Second Circle Demon is waiting to march upon Creation with dozens of lessers at their call.<br /> <br /> <b>Madness</b><br /> 1. For the next day, you are plagued by haunting apparitions out of the corners of your eyes, the shadows of pasts that never were and futures that will not be. You cannot spend Willpower during this time.<br /> 2. For the next day, you are haunted by the ghosts of your regrets. Spectral accusers shout your failings at you; your hands may drip with blood, or your reflection twist and mock you. You cannot spend or gain Willpower during this time. Alternatively, you may suffer from the first level for a week.<br /> 3. For the next day, you become prone to fits of inappropriate emotion- breaking suddenly into tears over dinner, laughing hysterically during a funeral, or falling asleep in a fight. Alternatively, instead of inappropriate emotions, fate may simply conspire against you, resulting in disastrous failure of what should be the easiest of tasks- most often when trying to warn someone of the consequences of their actions. Once per day, the Storyteller may opt to force one of your rolls to be a botch. They must declare this before you roll. Alternatively, you may suffer the first level for a month, or the second level for a week.<br /> 4. For the next day, you adopt one of your Resplendent Destiny personas. You are unable to act against your persona's intimacies, and believe the persona to be your true self. During this time, you are also unable to adopt a Resplendent Destiny; your fate is too fragmented to weave another atop it. Alternatively, you may suffer the first level for a season, the second for a month, or the third for a week.<br /> 5. You suffer one of the previous levels for (respectively) a week, a month, a season or a year.<br /> <br /> <b>Doom</b><br /> You gain a geas; a taboo of obligation or prohibition. Upon violation of this geas, your Doom falls, inflicting the specified amount of damage upon you. Until that time, it lurks, waiting and hungry. You and your Storyteller should work together to create an appropriate geas for you to labor under. This damage can also be safely dealt with; whenever you could remove a point of Paradox, you may instead remove a die of damage from your Doom. Once the damage is dealt, or if you reduce the damage to nothing, the geas is ended.<br /> <br /> Damage from Doom cannot be reduced by charms or armor. Fate will not be denied.<br /> <br /> 1. You will suffer 3 dice of bashing damage.<br /> 2. You will suffer either 6 dice of bashing damage, or 3 dice of lethal damage.<br /> 3. You will suffer either 10 dice of bashing damage, or 6 dice of lethal damage.<br /> 4. You will suffer 10 dice of lethal damage.<br /> 5. You will suffer 15 dice of lethal damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T12:32:48-07:00","id":924018,"title":"","content":"I will say that I like a lot of this <b>a lot</b> but there are two points that I dislike.<br /> <br /> 1) What happens when a Sidereal fulfills their Kismet? If their destiny is to &quot;Bring together two children of rival houses, both alike in dignity&quot; and they succeed... what happens? They're good and free forever then? If there a benefit to completing it other than removing an avenue of Paradox? And is that avenue gone forever when they complete it?<br /> <br /> 2) I am, and always will be, fundamentally opposed to limit breaks that can deal damage to the player, particularly enough damage to kill them. I will never support punishing a player with <i>Death </i>for role-playing in an interesting way. I don't want to turn this into a carrot/stick limit break argument, but I find Damage-As-Punishment to be boring at best, and a ridiculously unnecessary barrier to role-playing at worst.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T12:44:10-07:00","id":924028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/923952-sidereals-wfhl-traits-of-the-sidereal-exalted-paradox-and-kismet?p=924018#post924018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will say that I like a lot of this <b>a lot</b> but there are two points that I dislike.<br /> <br /> 1) What happens when a Sidereal fulfills their Kismet? If their destiny is to &quot;Bring together two children of rival houses, both alike in dignity&quot; and they succeed... what happens? They're good and free forever then? If there a benefit to completing it other than removing an avenue of Paradox? And is that avenue gone forever when they complete it?<br /> <br /> 2) I am, and always will be, fundamentally opposed to limit breaks that can deal damage to the player, particularly enough damage to kill them. I will never support punishing a player with <i>Death </i>for role-playing in an interesting way. I don't want to turn this into a carrot/stick limit break argument, but I find Damage-As-Punishment to be boring at best, and a ridiculously unnecessary barrier to role-playing at worst.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> 1) Two important lines:<br /> &quot;Finally, a Sidereal who permanently resolves her Kismet immediately reduces her Paradox to zero.&quot;<br /> &quot;Additionally, if a Sidereal\u2019s Kismet becomes impossible or meaningless, her player should work with the Storyteller to devise her new Kismet.&quot;<br /> <br /> 2) I mean, that's fair. I disagree, but with 15 (potentially) other points to distribute a maximum backlash of 10, I feel like the option for a Sidereal to get stuck with a sword of damoclese / final destination bullshit is thematic and interesting, without forcing damage as a mandatory consequence. If you disagree, then tell your ST 'Hey, I don't think damage is interesting, please focus on other backlash options'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T12:59:23-07:00","id":924039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/923952-sidereals-wfhl-traits-of-the-sidereal-exalted-paradox-and-kismet?p=924028#post924028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Two important lines:<br /> &quot;Finally, a Sidereal who permanently resolves her Kismet immediately reduces her Paradox to zero.&quot;<br /> &quot;Additionally, if a Sidereal\u2019s Kismet becomes impossible or meaningless, her player should work with the Storyteller to devise her new Kismet.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I admit I missed the first line, which helps a bit. The saw the second one, but &quot;meaningless&quot; doesn't seem to take my mind to the same place as &quot;resolved&quot; so I didn't really think it applied. I might include words to that end in there, but fair enough. So they gain a new Kismet when they achieve their former destiny. So they always have one. Got it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T13:04:12-07:00","id":924043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/923952-sidereals-wfhl-traits-of-the-sidereal-exalted-paradox-and-kismet?p=924039#post924039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I admit I missed the first line, which helps a bit. The saw the second one, but &quot;meaningless&quot; doesn't seem to take my mind to the same place as &quot;resolved&quot; so I didn't really think it applied. I might include words to that end in there, but fair enough. So they gain a new Kismet when they achieve their former destiny. So they always have one. Got it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Still implies a need for some tweaking to tighten up the language. Danke <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T15:14:45-07:00","id":924126,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure I like how hard it is to dump Paradox. It seems to be much harder to get rid of it than it is to gain it, and dumping it seems entirely dependent on taking a specific background or being abnormally good at your job.<br /> <br /> A Ronin without the Acquaintances background basically seems like they're fucked. Especially a <i>deliberately</i> rogue Ronin, who, if I'm reading this right, will roll two dice every single scene, because they're <i>always</i> deliberately thwarting the known will of Heaven, which is that Sidereals don't go rogue in the first place or that if they do, they report back for discipline and re-assignment.<br /> <br /> Unless that's intentional and part of your design space is that Ronin be constantly surrounded by backlash.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T17:30:32-07:00","id":924190,"title":"","content":"Hm. I think I'm going to need to add a sidebar to address what I mean by 'The known will of Heaven', because no, it's not meant to cause ronin and rogues to backlash like mad.<br /> <br /> It's more- okay. The 'default' Sidereals game is 'You go on zany troubleshooting missions from the Bureau of Destiny. Inevitably (because Sidereals is spy drama) orders from your home office will conflict with your personal desires, your code of ethics, or a secret mission that the home office doesn't know about.'<br /> <br /> The known will of heaven are your orders from the home office. Ronin who aren't getting orders from the home office don't have to worry about getting dox'd for violating said orders-they-don't-got. A Sidereal that's gone off the reservation doesn't have to worry about backlashes from violating the known will of Heaven, because they no longer get to *know* the will of Heaven. They might strongly *suspect* that it's Heaven's will that they turn themselves in, but that's not the same thing.<br /> <br /> But I think I'm going to have to think about how to capture that idea. Sidereals should be able to get orders in the field, so it can't be 'Only orders received in the Bureau of Destiny count as the revealed will of heaven'. It can't just be something any divinity or other spirit can fuck around with, or Sidereals are going to be boned. It has to be something verifiable on sight (or reasonably so). Hm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T17:50:41-07:00","id":924196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/923952-sidereals-wfhl-traits-of-the-sidereal-exalted-paradox-and-kismet?p=924190#post924190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I think I'm going to have to think about how to capture that idea. Sidereals should be able to get orders in the field, so it can't be 'Only orders received in the Bureau of Destiny count as the revealed will of heaven'. It can't just be something any divinity or other spirit can fuck around with, or Sidereals are going to be boned. It has to be something verifiable on sight (or reasonably so). Hm.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is how Sidereal Missions work in Hero:<br /> <br /> Sidereals traditionally get their missions in Red Envelopes. The majority of missions come from pattern spiders/the Maidens. The rest come from elder Sidereals. Elder Sidereals usually get more missions then they can personally handle, so they have offices of Gods and younger Sidereals that help them process the missions. <br /> <br /> Only the Sidereal and any god acting as their agent can open Red Envelopes missions addressed to them. Sidereals usually have a personal assistant/secretary type god who can act in their name while they are away. Similar to how a high level executive has a secretary that answers emails in their name. However, like a secretary puts their initials on the bottom of a letter. While it is not in their best interest for a god to screw over a Sidereal, it has happened before, so there is a paper trail going back to a Sidereal's godly agent. This godly agent is represented as a Retainer on the Sidereal's character sheet. As an ST, I wouldn't screw around with a PC's godly personal assistant unless the PC is a total dick to them. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-02T09:24:32-07:00","id":924907,"title":"","content":"Additional sidebar:<br /> <b><span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">--Sidebar: The Will of Heaven--</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The known will of Heaven is another way of saying the plans of the Bureau of Destiny has made for Creation; among the Sidereal Exalted, it usually refers to missions assigned by the Bureau to the Agents of Heaven. Sidereals are often, but not always, told of these missions in briefings by various gods in the Bureau of Destiny- but they can also learn the broad overview or any changes made while in the field by studying the omens and using their anima power (p. XX)</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The known will of Heaven should always focus on some result or consequence, and potentially some constraints upon that result, but should not direct how the Sidereal is to accomplish the goal. The known will of Heaven should never direct a Sidereal\u2019s actions, but rather provide them with goals to accomplish. </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A Sidereal should never accidentally or unknowingly gain Paradox from failing to uphold or acting against the known will of Heaven.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Ronin and rogue Sidereals will not generally be assigned missions, and therefore not know the will of Heaven, and thus cannot gain Paradox by acting against it. However, such disloyalty also bars them from accessing Heaven\u2019s resources and makes casting Astrological Projections a far more daunting task. Some will study the omens and use their anima to determine Heaven\u2019s plans- but knowing what is intended binds them as agents to see it done, or risk Paradox and backlash.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#666666\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">--End Sidebar--</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":169,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","user":"wastevens","date":". 07-02-2016, 12:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}